{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1107828-new-gods","id":1107828,"title":"New gods?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-06-25T18:00:42-07:00","id":1107828,"title":"New gods?","content":"Ok folks, it seems to me (might be wrong, but it's seems so from the internet) that the new gods in American Gods built up a big fanbase. Is it right? Is it true for you? If so, could you explain your thought process on the thing?<br /> <br /> To be true, my puzzlement is quite great. I get the &quot;tech and modernity is keeeewl and hip&quot; angle, but honestly, I hated those guys in the book and hate them in the series. Not because the old gods (not <i>those</i> old gods) are good guys, but simply because the new ones and their vision of the world gave me the creep.<br /> <br /> Why am I posting this here? Because I think it resembles the ever-recurring &quot;why people like the Technocracy/Technocracy vs. the Traditions&quot; question we're all too familiar with, although I think the new gods have even less redeeming qualities than the Technocracy. On the other hand, they are a great inspiration for portraying Control, I think.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If nothing worked, then let's think!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","name":"PM\u00e1rk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-25T19:11:49-07:00","id":1107849,"title":"","content":"I'm hoping as they expand on the book material for the show we might get to see some other New Gods besides &quot;Mr World&quot;, Technical Boy, and Media.<br /> <br /> - Sam, God of American Nationalism &amp; the State; former leader of the New Gods unseated by Mr World (God of Globalism), playing into the Nietzchian concept of the State as the &quot;New Idol&quot;. Greatly resents Mr World so is a fence sitter in-play in the conflict.<br /> <br /> - Mr Bull &amp; Mr Bear, twin gods of the Market. Mr Bull is prayed to for his benevolence. Mr Bear is appeased for fear of drawing his wrath.<br /> <br /> Given how this season ended, a deity of bio-science and agrobusiness would be appropriate to show up (I know Technical Boy is broadly spoken of a &quot;God of Technology&quot;, but that's clearly just in the &quot;Tech Industry&quot; sense of Technology. Prayers for bio-science to solve a famine are going to go elsewhere). Give her a good long rant equating Wednesday and crew with anti-vaxxers and GMO-fear-mongering.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-25T20:00:58-07:00","id":1107858,"title":"","content":"I pretty much dropped American Gods right after reading the part where a dude is devoured by a chicks Vagina. Never really felt the urge to pick the book back up so I don't really know how much the new gods align with the Technocracy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-25T21:14:33-07:00","id":1107878,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enginseer-42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1107828-new-gods?p=1107858#post1107858\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I pretty much dropped American Gods right after reading the part where a dude is devoured by a chicks Vagina. Never really felt the urge to pick the book back up so I don't really know how much the new gods align with the Technocracy.</div> </div> </div> </div>Really? Well, different sensibilities, I guess, but I think it's a damn fine book and very Mage-y (and also a great inspirational material, listed in basically nearly every Mage book since it was published).<br /> <br /> The new gods are pretty much avatars of spirits (Incarnae-level, maybe) of concepts the technocracy hold dear, or make great use of them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If nothing worked, then let's think!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","name":"PM\u00e1rk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-25T22:13:31-07:00","id":1107900,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enginseer-42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1107828-new-gods?p=1107858#post1107858\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I pretty much dropped American Gods right after reading the part where a dude is devoured by a chicks Vagina. Never really felt the urge to pick the book back up so I don't really know how much the new gods align with the Technocracy.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well wouldn't recommend the show then. My only issue with that scene is calling her Bilquis instead of something more directly Inanna related, bringing on various baggage about the interpretations of the Queen of Sheba through history. But sexual human sacrifice is pretty mythicaly on point for a primordial fertility goddess like Gaiman was getting at.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-26T04:33:58-07:00","id":1107970,"title":"","content":"I get what he was going for. But I am generally disappointed when it seems like sex is artificially crammed into tons of places in a book.<br /> <br /> It always felt to me as if they're trying to give it a sense of maturity by involving things that are adults only. But then take it too far and lead to it seeming the opposite.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-26T05:52:03-07:00","id":1107996,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enginseer-42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1107828-new-gods?p=1107970#post1107970\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I get what he was going for. But I am generally disappointed when it seems like sex is artificially crammed into tons of places in a book.<br /> <br /> It always felt to me as if they're trying to give it a sense of maturity by involving things that are adults only. But then take it too far and lead to it seeming the opposite.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've definitely seen that happen with other authors, but Gaiman rarely does anything without reason. Which is not to say everything he adds is necessary or that he never takes anything to excess, but if something is in his books it usually has greater meaning than false maturity.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-29T01:36:23-07:00","id":1109150,"title":"","content":"One of the concepts is that worship can take many different forms - so while the old gods were fed with sacrifice and prayer, the new gods are fed with time and attention. <br /> Plus, just like mage, it's a story of its time - the new gods seem clunky to us now because the things they represent have changed so much since then. <br /> <br /> On the subject of sex in the book and show, try this for an alternative view: <a href=\"http://io9.gizmodo.com/every-show-should-handle-sex-like-american-gods-1795475389\" target=\"_blank\">http://io9.gizmodo.com/every-show-sh...ods-1795475389</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13587-eyrelliah","name":"Eyrelliah","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13587_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"92"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-29T04:52:42-07:00","id":1109184,"title":"","content":"It immediately stuck me how <i>Mage </i>the American Gods seems to be. You can merge the 2 without changing much at all. Fortunately for the old gods, psychology shows that humans are basically illogical mysterious beings so faith in them will never be gone entirely. To be fair, NOW should be a way better time for them then in the centuries past. Media had brought many to the forefront of attention, religious freedom lets cults flourish with impunity and large population ensures they can move undetected and amass followers without fighting each other. Really, there are still millions of people worshiping old gods and ample opportunities to collect sacrifices without rising questions, like Vulcan. The wicca movement should also have plaid in their hands. Would love to see if there are mages in AG, judging by Shadow changing weather - there should be. <br /> pity that due to general consensus it is not PC to discuss how Middle east would play in all this. I only remember 1 game (The Cabal) that blatantly admitted that Djinn controlled the fundamentalists to push against western influence and mystic elements (local Hermetics) supporting them. Was a pretty interesting plotline. Would love to at least see what powers moved the Soviets and North Corea. Or who holds current China. <br /> BTW, The cabal has an interesting take on ascension war. Hermetics teamed up with Mummies, Vampires, Shapeshifters and some other nasties and kicked everyone else's teeth in. They also invented science as a means to distract Masses from the real universe of magic. To be fair they tried several times to go public before doing that - it never ended well. So they wen't &quot;fuck it. let the mundanes play with the primitive alchemy&quot; and kept the magic on low, but accessible level sins then.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4340-warpwind","name":"Warpwind","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4340_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"608"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-29T09:19:11-07:00","id":1109269,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1107828-new-gods?p=1107849#post1107849\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm hoping as they expand on the book material for the show we might get to see some other New Gods besides &quot;Mr World&quot;, Technical Boy, and Media.<br /> <br /> - Sam, God of American Nationalism &amp; the State; former leader of the New Gods unseated by Mr World (God of Globalism), playing into the Nietzchian concept of the State as the &quot;New Idol&quot;. Greatly resents Mr World so is a fence sitter in-play in the conflict.<br /> <br /> - Mr Bull &amp; Mr Bear, twin gods of the Market. Mr Bull is prayed to for his benevolence. Mr Bear is appeased for fear of drawing his wrath.<br /> <br /> Given how this season ended, a deity of bio-science and agrobusiness would be appropriate to show up (I know Technical Boy is broadly spoken of a &quot;God of Technology&quot;, but that's clearly just in the &quot;Tech Industry&quot; sense of Technology. Prayers for bio-science to solve a famine are going to go elsewhere). Give her a good long rant equating Wednesday and crew with anti-vaxxers and GMO-fear-mongering.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which would be things such a deity would be deity of, since those are beliefs. Having such a god taking a pro-vaccination or less hysterical GMO-Luddite stance would be like Media raging against the effects of her own goodies. <br /> <br /> Besides, is &quot;bioscience&quot; a coherent thing belief-wise? It seems more likely there would be a god of consumption/eating (from McDonalds to the Food Network to fad diets and obesity) and one of medicine, and so on (probably). And such gods be heavily influenced by popular cultural ideas of their portfolios more than anything else.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-29T09:32:59-07:00","id":1109280,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1107828-new-gods?p=1107996#post1107996\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I've definitely seen that happen with other authors, but Gaiman rarely does anything without reason. Which is not to say everything he adds is necessary or that he never takes anything to excess, but if something is in his books it usually has greater meaning than false maturity.</div> </div> </div> </div>Agreed. And something you don't get from a lot of sanitized myths more people read is how laden with sex they are. (The &quot;real&quot; story in the Osiris cycle, for example, or the Hymn to Inanna.)<br /> <br /> If anything, Gaiman was pretty tame about it, comparatively speaking. If you're telling a &quot;new myth&quot; in the style of the old, not like Disney or D'aulaire or Bullfinch would, you are going to have sex in there. A lot of it and more graphic than most modern audiences are comfortable with.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-29T09:42:50-07:00","id":1109285,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1107828-new-gods?p=1107900#post1107900\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well wouldn't recommend the show then. My only issue with that scene is calling her Bilquis instead of something more directly Inanna related, bringing on various baggage about the interpretations of the Queen of Sheba through history. But sexual human sacrifice is pretty mythicaly on point for a primordial fertility goddess like Gaiman was getting at.</div> </div> </div> </div>She's not supposed to be Inanna or Astarte or Ishtar. She's supposed to be the goddess associated with the Sabaen period in what is now Yemen and pre-Aksumite Damot in modern Ethiopea, probably more explicitly the later than the former, as female primacy/equality was more of a &quot;thing&quot; there, but maybe not (the scenes depict her and her followers as more explicitly African than Arabian, but she is seen to be upset at the demolition of a temple in Yemen, so, &lt;shrug&gt;). Which in turn associates her with the legend/myth of biblical Sheba that he was using for the name. He's definitely taking liberties by inventing some mythology for a very vague figure, but, as you said, he was going for an archetype and there's no reason for it NOT to fit (and, considering his desire to avoid all things Graeco-Roman combined with a tacit Old World but not Eastern Old World focus, it's as good a card toss into the hat as any).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-29T09:50:32-07:00","id":1109288,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Warpwind</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1107828-new-gods?p=1109184#post1109184\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Would love to see if there are mages in AG, judging by Shadow changing weather - there should be.</div> </div> </div> </div>In the books and subsequent stories, it's pretty obvious Shadow is god-like in many ways. Probably Odin's son. In a later story it's revealed that Shadow isn't even his real name. Or, at least, it's not the name on his passport....<br /> <br /> Insofar as it seeming like it could be Mage. Well.... Mage is pretty wide open in many ways and amendable, as a set of rules, to being used for other ideas. And there are some explicit parallels between the Technocracy vs. (some of) the Traditions. But it's a serious adaptation. Trying to accomodate issues like vulgar and coincidental and Paradox will need some serious tweaking. Games like Scion were designed from the outset to try to deal with this (explicitly citing American Gods as a major inspiration) and it worked to a degree. (And probably might better with the redo. I dunno. I'll never find out as I'm done with Scion.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-29T09:54:58-07:00","id":1109292,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1107828-new-gods?p=1109288#post1109288\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Insofar as it seeming like it could be Mage. Well.... Mage is pretty wide open in many ways and amendable, as a set of rules, to being used for other ideas. And there are some explicit parallels between the Technocracy vs. (some of) the Traditions. But it's a serious adaptation. Trying to accomodate issues like vulgar and coincidental and Paradox will need some serious tweaking. Games like Scion were designed from the outset to try to deal with this (explicitly citing American Gods as a major inspiration) and it worked to a degree. (And probably might better with the redo. I dunno. I'll never find out as I'm done with Scion.)</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bwhat? No no no. I don't mean using AG as mages. Keep them gods. Don't spirits gain/loose in power with human worship in MtA? some old gods may well be going around in the real world trying to regain power and new spirits/gods are born.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4340-warpwind","name":"Warpwind","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4340_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"608"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-29T10:04:45-07:00","id":1109297,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Warpwind</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1107828-new-gods?p=1109292#post1109292\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> \u200bwhat? No no no. I don't mean using AG as mages. Keep them gods. Don't spirits gain/loose in power with human worship in MtA? some old gods may well be going around in the real world trying to regain power and new spirits/gods are born.</div> </div> </div> </div>That doesn't have to be a thing in Mage and probably isn't for the most part. Middle Umbra spirits don't need people to believe in them to get Gnosis. They don't disappear like Tinkerbell if no one is clapping hands in their honor. High Umbra is more likely to have some affect from belief, but it doesn't have to be anything 